IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.03 (illness, injury or quarantine) and
-- 152.04 (pregnancy), with the two reduction rules that sections 152.03 to 152.062 all repeat.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- Weeks are identified by the DATE of their Sunday (keel convention); a period is a `Period of days` whose
-- first day is a Sunday and whose last day is a Saturday. The Regulations are never quoted: what they prescribe is
-- a plain input with "out of range: reg N (piece X)". Dates: no enactment or commencement date in these sections.

§ `152.03 Benefits -- illness, injury or quarantine`

-- Subsection (1), with the exception of (1.1): the person who is unable to work because of a prescribed illness,
-- injury or quarantine is entitled while unable to work, if they ceased to work because of it and would otherwise
-- be working; the person to whom benefits are payable under any of ss 152.05 to 152.062 is entitled even if they did
-- not cease to work because of it and would not be working anyway. Either way the person must have the illness and
-- be unable to work for that reason ("while unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason").
-- src:2164 | 152.03 (1) Subject to this Part, a self-employed person who ceases to work as a self-employed person because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine and who would be otherwise working, is entitled to receive benefits while unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason.
-- src:2166 | (1.1) A self-employed person to whom benefits are payable under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062 is entitled to benefits under subsection (1) even though the person did not cease to work as a self-employed person because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine and would not be working even without the illness, injury or quarantine.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.03(1) and (1.1) (src:2164) (src:2166)
GIVEN `has a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 40(4) (piece er3)
      `is unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ceased to work as a self-employed person because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would be otherwise working` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work` IF
        `has a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `is unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason`
    AND (    (`ceased to work as a self-employed person because of it` AND `would be otherwise working`)
          OR `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062`)

-- Subsection (4): a person other than one referred to in (1.1) is not entitled if, were it not for the prescribed
-- illness, injury or quarantine, they would be deemed in accordance with the regulations to be not working.
-- src:2172 | (4) A self-employed person, other than one referred to in subsection (1.1), is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1) if, were it not for the prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, the self-employed person would be deemed, in accordance with the regulations, to be not working.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.03(4) (src:2172)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine the person would be deemed in accordance with the regulations to be not working` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 30.2 (piece er2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)` IF
        NOT (`benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062`)
    AND `were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine the person would be deemed in accordance with the regulations to be not working`

-- The two together: entitled under (1) or (1.1) and not excluded by (4).
-- src:2164 | 152.03 (1) Subject to this Part, a self-employed person who ceases to work as a self-employed person because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine and who would be otherwise working, is entitled to receive benefits while unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason.
-- src:2166 | (1.1) A self-employed person to whom benefits are payable under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062 is entitled to benefits under subsection (1) even though the person did not cease to work as a self-employed person because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine and would not be working even without the illness, injury or quarantine.
-- src:2172 | (4) A self-employed person, other than one referred to in subsection (1.1), is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1) if, were it not for the prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, the self-employed person would be deemed, in accordance with the regulations, to be not working.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.03(1), (1.1) and (4) (src:2164) (src:2166) (src:2172)
GIVEN `has a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ceased to work as a self-employed person because of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `would be otherwise working` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062` IS A BOOLEAN
      `were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine the person would be deemed in accordance with the regulations to be not working` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.03 entitled to benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine` IF
        `s 152.03(1) and (1.1) a self-employed person is entitled to benefits while unable to work`
            `has a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` `is unable to work as a self-employed person for that reason`
            `ceased to work as a self-employed person because of it` `would be otherwise working`
            `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062`
    AND NOT (`s 152.03(4) a self-employed person is not entitled to benefits under subsection (1)`
                `benefits are payable to the person under any of sections 152.05 to 152.062`
                `were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine the person would be deemed in accordance with the regulations to be not working`)

§§ `The reductions that sections 152.03 to 152.062 repeat`

-- Where benefits are payable under this Part for the reasons of the section and allowances, money or other benefits
-- are payable for the same reasons under a provincial law, the benefits under this Part are "reduced or eliminated as
-- prescribed". Six subsections say it in the same words; one rule serves all six. The reduction is the Regulations'
-- (regs 76.36 to 76.42 for ss 152.04 and 152.05, piece er4; none found for the other four), so it is an input, and
-- "eliminated" is a reduction as large as the benefit. The result cannot be below zero (fork F7).
-- src:2168 | (2) If benefits are payable to a self-employed person as a result of illness, injury or quarantine and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person for that illness, injury or quarantine under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the person under this Part shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
-- src:2184 | (3) When benefits are payable to a self-employed person for unemployment caused by pregnancy and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person for that pregnancy under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the self-employed person under this Part shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
-- src:2219 | (11) If benefits are payable to a self-employed person for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person for the same reasons under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the self-employed person under this Part are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
-- src:2276 | (9) If benefits are payable to a self-employed person for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the person under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
-- src:2313 | (11) When benefits are payable to a self-employed person for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the person under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
-- src:2346 | (9) When benefits are payable to a self-employed person for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons, the benefits payable to the person under this section shall be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.03(2), s 152.04(3), s 152.05(11), s 152.06(9), s 152.061(11), s 152.062(9) (src:2168) (src:2184) (src:2219) (src:2276) (src:2313) (src:2346)
GIVEN `the weekly benefits otherwise payable under this Part` IS A NUMBER
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person for the same reason under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction prescribed` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: regs 76.36 to 76.42 (piece er4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.03(2), 152.04(3), 152.05(11), 152.06(9), 152.061(11) and 152.062(9) benefits after the reduction prescribed for benefits payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the person for the same reason under a provincial law`
    THEN max 0 (`the weekly benefits otherwise payable under this Part` MINUS `the reduction prescribed`)
    ELSE `the weekly benefits otherwise payable under this Part`

-- "there shall be deducted from those benefits any allowances, money or other benefits payable to the person for that
-- week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer's
-- premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1)". Subject to s 152.18(3)
-- (undeclared earnings), which is a separate rule in ei5-payment. The result cannot be below zero (fork F7).
-- src:2170 | (3) Subject to subsection 152.18(3), if benefits are payable under this section to a self-employed person for a week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from those benefits any allowances, money or other benefits payable to the person for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer’s premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1).
-- src:2188 | (4) Subject to subsection 152.18(3), if benefits are payable under this section to a self-employed person for a week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from those benefits any allowances, money or other benefits payable to the person for that week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by an employer and in respect of which the employer’s premium has been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.03(3) and s 152.04(4) (src:2170) (src:2188)
GIVEN `the benefits payable for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the person for that week under such a plan` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: s 69(1) (piece ei3), regs 60 to 74 (piece er4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.03(3) and 152.04(4) benefits after the deduction of allowances payable under a plan whose employer's premium has been reduced` IS
    max 0 (`the benefits payable for the week` MINUS `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to the person for that week under such a plan`)

§ `152.04 Benefits -- pregnancy`

-- src:2174 | 152.04 (1) Subject to this Part, benefits are payable to a self-employed person who proves her pregnancy.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.04(1) (src:2174)
GIVEN `proves her pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 41(1) (piece er3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.04(1) benefits are payable because of pregnancy` IF
    `proves her pregnancy`

-- The period: it begins with the earlier of the week twelve weeks before the week of expected confinement and the week
-- of confinement, and ends seventeen weeks after the later of the week of expected confinement and the week of
-- confinement. Read as whole weeks: the period begins on the Sunday of its first week and ends on the Saturday of
-- the week seventeen weeks after the later week (fork F8). While confinement has not yet occurred, the week of
-- confinement is taken to be the week it is expected, so the period is the one the expected date gives (fork F9).
-- src:2176 | (2) Subject to section 152.14, benefits are payable to a self-employed person under this section for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:2177 | (a) that begins the earlier of
-- src:2178 | (i) 12 weeks before the week in which her confinement is expected, and
-- src:2179 | (ii) the week in which her confinement occurs; and
-- src:2180 | (b) that ends 17 weeks after the later of
-- src:2181 | (i) the week in which her confinement is expected, and
-- src:2182 | (ii) the week in which her confinement occurs.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.04(2) (src:2176-2182)
GIVEN `the day on which her confinement is expected` IS A DATE
      `the day on which her confinement occurs, if it has occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.04(2) the period for which benefits are payable because of pregnancy` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day of the period`, `the last day of the period`
    WHERE
        `the week of the expected confinement` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which her confinement is expected`
        `the week of the confinement` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day on which her confinement occurs, if it has occurred`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the week of the expected confinement`
            WHEN JUST d THEN `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` d
        `the week 12 weeks before the week of the expected confinement` MEANS
            `the week of the expected confinement` PLUS (0 MINUS (`weeks as days` 12))
        `the first day of the period` MEANS
            IF `the week of the confinement` LESS THAN `the week 12 weeks before the week of the expected confinement`
            THEN `the week of the confinement`
            ELSE `the week 12 weeks before the week of the expected confinement`
        `the later of the two weeks` MEANS
            IF `the week of the confinement` GREATER THAN `the week of the expected confinement`
            THEN `the week of the confinement`
            ELSE `the week of the expected confinement`
        `the last day of the period` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`the later of the two weeks` PLUS (`weeks as days` 17))

-- Subsection (3.1): for serving the waiting period of s 152.15, the week immediately before the period in (2) is deemed
-- to be a week included in that period.
-- src:2186 | (3.1) With regard to serving the waiting period under section 152.15, the week that immediately precedes the period described in subsection (2) is deemed to be a week that is included in that period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.04(3.1) (src:2186)
GIVEN `the period described in subsection (2)` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.04(3.1) the period, for serving the waiting period, with the week that immediately precedes it` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`the period described in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period` PLUS (0 MINUS 7)),
                        `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `last day of the period`

-- Subsections (5) and (6): if the child born of the pregnancy is hospitalized, the period is extended by the number of
-- weeks of hospitalization, and the extended period ends no later than 52 weeks after the week of confinement (the
-- Saturday of the week fifty-two weeks after it: the same reading as (2)).
-- src:2190 | (5) If a child who is born of the self-employed person’s pregnancy is hospitalized, the period for which benefits are payable under subsection (2) shall be extended by the number of weeks during which the child is hospitalized.
-- src:2192 | (6) The extended period shall end no later than 52 weeks after the week of confinement.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.04(5) and (6) (src:2190) (src:2192)
GIVEN `the period described in subsection (2)` IS A `Period of days`
      `the day on which her confinement occurred` IS A DATE
      `the number of weeks during which the child is hospitalized` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 152.04(5) and (6) the period extended because the child is hospitalized` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `first day of the period`,
                        `the last day of the extended period`
    WHERE
        `the last day of the extended period` MEANS
            IF `the extended end before the limit` LESS THAN `the latest permitted last day`
            THEN `the extended end before the limit`
            ELSE `the latest permitted last day`
        `the extended end before the limit` MEANS
            `the period described in subsection (2)`'s `last day of the period` PLUS (`weeks as days` `the number of weeks during which the child is hospitalized`)
        `the latest permitted last day` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which her confinement occurred` PLUS (`weeks as days` 52))
